<BaseLayout title="Corrections — Freighthub" description="How Freighthub handles errors, what counts as a correction, and the log of changes made to published pages.">
  <article>
    <h1>Corrections</h1>
    <p class="article-meta">Policy and log · Last reviewed 11 November 2026</p>

    <h2>Our policy</h2>
    <p>Freighthub publishes analysis, not a live quotation service. Errors are inevitable, and the useful response is a visible one.</p>
    <p>When we find an error, we:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Correct the page</strong> as soon as the error is confirmed.</li>
      <li><strong>Add a dated line to the update log</strong> at the bottom of the page.</li>
      <li><strong>Record the correction here</strong> if it changes a material fact, a range or a judgement.</li>
      <li><strong>Remove or rewrite the claim</strong> if it cannot be supported.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>We distinguish between a <strong>correction</strong> (a factual error, a wrong number, a misnamed authority or a broken source), a <strong>clarification</strong> (wording that was accurate but ambiguous) and an <strong>update</strong> (new information that changes the picture, even if the original was correct).</p>
    <p>We do not silently delete a page to avoid a correction. If a page is withdrawn, the withdrawal is noted.</p>

    <h2>How to report an error</h2>
    <p>Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Include the page URL, the sentence and, if possible, the source that shows the error. We aim to acknowledge within five working days.</p>

    <h2>Correction log</h2>
    <h3>11 November 2026 — battery sector</h3>
    <p><strong>Page:</strong> <a href="/sectors/batteries/">Batteries sector</a><br />
    <strong>Change:</strong> Corrected the acronym "SCoB" to "SCoC" (Shipment Certificate of Conformity).<br />
    <strong>Type:</strong> Correction — terminology error, no change to meaning.</p>

    <h3>11 November 2026 — launch baseline</h3>
    <p><strong>Pages:</strong> all pages published in the compressed completion sprint.<br />
    <strong>Change:</strong> First publication. No prior published claims to correct.<br />
    <strong>Type:</strong> Launch note.</p>

    <h2>What we do not log</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Copy edits that do not change meaning.</li>
      <li>Formatting changes.</li>
      <li>Updates to internal links.</li>
      <li>Changes to the "last reviewed" date when no substantive content changed.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>A note on ranges</h2>
    <p>Most of our cost and transit figures are ranges, not point estimates. A range is not a correction target unless it is clearly wrong or unsupported. If a range is stale, we update the page and note the new market conditions in the update log.</p>

